  "Scenes.Owca.OwcaMainScreenOn.TavernAppearsOpen": "[pg]A tavern appears to be open; various Owca folk are drinking and chatting in it. They give you friendly waves when you make eye contact."
  "Scenes.Owca.OwcaMainScreenOn.ThisTimeFullyUnderstand": "[pg]This time you fully understand the consequences of another sacrifice. Do you comply?"
  "Scenes.Owca.OwcaMainScreenOn.VillageRatherSmall": " The village is rather small. A dozen humble thatched cottages are standing here and there, linked by dirt tracks and enclosed with small palisades. There seems to be very little activity."
  "Scenes.Owca.OwcaMainScreenOn.VillageShowsUnusualSigns": "The village shows unusual signs of activity. As you walk down the main road, people are all looking at you uncomfortably. Some try to approach you but back off awkwardly at the last moment. You don't understand until you stumble upon Rebecc, who seems on better terms with you than the rest of the village; she is displaying a worried face."
  "Scenes.Owca.OwcaMainScreenOn.VillagersAcceptPresence": "Villagers seem to accept your presence without comment now; though none go out of their way to greet you, neither do they avoid doing so when you pass by."
  "Scenes.Owca.OwcaMainScreenOn.VillagersGreetFriendly": "Villagers greet you with a friendly smile as you arrive. Some approach you and thank you for what you've done, before leaving awkwardly. They're obviously not used to strangers."
  "Scenes.Owca.OwcaMainScreenOn.VillagersGreetYou": "Villagers greet you as you arrive, praising your courage and your heroism. People shake your hands or ask you to kiss them, as if they hoped your nobility were somehow contagious. Once they're done complimenting and flattering you in every way possible, they leave you to your business."
  "Scenes.Owca.OwcaMainScreenOn.VillagersLookUncomfortably": "Villagers keep looking at you uncomfortably; no one seems to be willing to talk to you apart from Rebecc, your friend."
  "Scenes.Owca.OwcaMainScreenOn.VillagersOpenly": "Villagers here appear to be openly hostile. You keep hearing muffled whispers as you pass by, and people look at you rancorously. They don't bother you, though."
